# Contact form email settings: a template only (no real details here). The real settings go in .env.
#
# Copy this file to a file named .env and fill in the values. On the hosting, put .env ONE FOLDER
# ABOVE public_html (for example /home/<cpanel-user>/.env) so it can never be opened in a browser; it is
# read by site/send-enquiry.php. On this PC, keep .env in this project folder: the local preview
# (Start website.bat, src/preview-mailer.js) and php -S read it from here.
# Never upload .env into public_html and never share it. .env is in .gitignore.

# SMTP server that sends the email (cPanel: Email Accounts > Connect Devices shows these)
#SMTP_HOST=mail.brand-image.co.in
# 465 with ssl, or 587 with tls
#SMTP_PORT=465
#SMTP_SECURE=ssl
#SMTP_USER=cs@brand-image.co.in
#SMTP_PASS=

# Sender shown on the enquiry email (should be the SMTP account itself)
#MAIL_FROM=cs@brand-image.co.in
#MAIL_FROM_NAME=Brand Image Website

# Who receives the enquiries: one address, or several separated by commas
#MAIL_TO=cs@brand-image.co.in

# Google reCAPTCHA v2 ("I'm not a robot" checkbox) on the contact form. Create the keys at
# https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin : type reCAPTCHA v2, "I'm not a robot" Checkbox; domains brand-image.co.in
# and localhost. The site key is public (built into the page: run npm run build after setting it); the secret
# is private. Without both there is no captcha.
#RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
#RECAPTCHA_SECRET=
